# uno/test/golden/state-transitions-v1.hex
#
# Consensus-binding golden fixtures for the §4.3 verify + apply pipeline
# (§12 P.3 of doc/uno-workchain.md).
#
# Each record pins one (UnoShardState X, Transfer Y) → (UnoShardState X', verdict)
# tuple. The consumer test (uno/test/test-state-transition-golden.cpp) parses
# this file and asserts byte-equality against the running implementation.
#
# Format:
#   record_id=<int, monotonically increasing from 1>
#   label=<short-human-label>
#   verdict=<Ok | one of VerifyResult::* names from uno/core/compute-phase.h>
#   pre_state=<hex byte blob; canonical UnoShardState serialisation>
#   transfer=<hex byte blob; canonical §4.1 wire format>
#   post_state=<hex byte blob; present ONLY when verdict == Ok>
#   ---
#
# Empty hex values are written as empty strings on the right of the `=`.
#
# --- CURRENT STATE (P.7 scaffold) -------------------------------------------
# The pre_state / transfer / post_state blobs below are intentionally empty
# placeholders at P.7 scaffold time because:
#
#   a. UnoShardState's canonical byte serialisation (uno/core/cell-state.cpp)
#      is not yet finalised end-to-end — some sub-objects still SKIP
#      in-progress cases (commitment-tree frontier for non-power-of-two
#      position counts; nullifier-set rehash on LRU eviction).
#   b. The Transfer wire encoder (uno/core/transaction.cpp :: encode_transfer)
#      currently only handles the 1-spend/1-output shape.
#   c. The Plonky3 Transfer AIR (§4.2 claims 1-8) is in P.2; without real
#      proof bytes the fixture would need fake proofs, and a fake proof
#      pinned in the consensus golden file is worse than a SKIP.
#
# Pre-populating the expected post_state hex NOW with placeholder bytes would
# bake in wrong bytes that the first real-AIR run would spuriously fail on.
# Per the N-P7 scope note: "Deterministic GTEST_SKIP is preferred over
# hardcoded fixtures with wrong proofs." — we honour that here.
#
# Once P.2 AIR lands and encode_transfer supports 1..4 shapes:
#   1. Regenerate blobs via a dedicated fixture-gen CLI in tosctl.
#   2. Paste the resulting hex into the respective record fields.
#   3. Remove the "blobs are empty" text from this header.
#   4. Bump the file version suffix (v1 → v2) IF any existing record's
#      pre_state / transfer / post_state *changes*. Appending new records
#      stays at v1.
#
# --- Records ----------------------------------------------------------------

